---
import Docs from '@/layouts/docs.astro';
import Snippet from '@/components/product/Snippet.astro';
import Integrations from '@/components/product/Integrations.astro';
import { httpRequest } from '@/data/examples';
---

<Docs title="API, SDKs & CLI reference">
  <div class="doc-title">
    <span class="section-kicker">INTEGRATE / REFERENCE</span>
    <h1>Choose an interface.</h1>
    <p>Use HTTP across languages, the CLI from scripts, the TypeScript SDK in Node.js, or the engine in Rust.</p>
  </div>

  <h2>AuthZEN HTTP</h2>
  <p><code>POST /access/v1/evaluation</code> accepts the following starter-schema request. Context includes args and session; required arguments vary by action.</p>
  <Snippet code={JSON.stringify(httpRequest, null, 2)} lang="json" title="Single evaluation request" />
  <Snippet code={'{"decision": true}'} lang="json" title="Successful allow response" />
  <p>The response contains a boolean decision and optional reason/context. Proceed only on a successful response with decision exactly true. A false decision is a normal authorization result. Authentication errors, malformed responses, timeouts, and HTTP failures must stop the tool.</p>

  <h2>Batch evaluation</h2>
  <p><code>POST /access/v1/evaluations</code> accepts an evaluations array, capped at 100. Optional evaluation_semantics supports execute_all, deny_on_first_deny, and permit_on_first_permit. Each nested evaluation may include its own entities array; entity sets are evaluated independently and malformed entities fail the batch. The response contains an evaluations array; early-exit modes can return fewer results than requests.</p>

  <h2>Integration examples</h2>
  <Integrations />

  <h2>TypeScript SDK behavior</h2>
  <p>Build with <code>pnpm install</code> and <code>pnpm --filter agentguard build</code> at the repository root. The package exports Client, Principal, Action, AuthorizationDenied, StepUpRequired, and CLIUnavailable. It wraps a local Node.js CLI process; it is not a browser SDK or remote HTTP client.</p>
  <p>Existing synchronous methods remain available for scripts. In web servers and other concurrent Node.js applications, use the asynchronous <code>Client.logTailAsync</code> and <code>Client.delegateAsync</code> variants to avoid blocking the event loop. Async CLI operations default to a 30-second timeout, allow at most 8 concurrent children per Client, and cap combined output at 8 MiB. Configure these limits with <code>ClientOptions.timeoutMs</code> and <code>ClientOptions.maxConcurrentCliProcesses</code>.</p>
  <p><code>Client.check</code> throws on deny. <code>Client.authorize</code> returns a Decision unless check is requested. The SDK can interpret a step_up field in a denied response, but the current core/server path does not emit a step-up decision. BearerToken is passed as AGENTGUARD_BEARER; the local CLI does not validate or forward it to a remote PDP. No SDK option currently produces DPoP proofs.</p>

  <h2>gRPC</h2>
  <p>Enable the loopback listener with <code>--grpc-listen 127.0.0.1:9443</code>. The repository-defined service is agentguard.v1.AccessEvaluation/Evaluation. It mirrors the HTTP single evaluation with context_json and entities_json strings. Use the <a href="https://github.com/sachncs/agent-guard/blob/master/crates/agentguard-server/proto/agentguard.proto">checked-in protobuf</a> to generate clients. The listener is plaintext and does not constitute a standardized AuthZEN gRPC protocol.</p>

  <h2>CLI commands</h2>
  <div class="docs-table">
    {[
      ['init', 'Create a schema and broad development starter policies.'],
      ['validate / schema', 'Validate policies or inspect the schema.'],
      ['authorize / sim', 'Evaluate a CLI request; sim uses the authorization path and writes audit by default.'],
      ['delegate / verify', 'Mint and verify delegation tokens; these do not enforce scopes on a tool.'],
      ['log tail / log dump', 'Read decision records.'],
      ['audit verify / export', 'Verify chained records or export JSONL, CEF, LEEF, ECS.'],
      ['audit sar / erase / rotate', 'Subject lookup, pseudonymization, and file rotation. Erasure changes records and invalidates the original chain.'],
      ['gen', 'Generate a policy through a configured LLM provider and validate it. Review output before installing.'],
      ['doctor', 'Check the local store and audit setup.'],
    ].map(([name, body]) => (
      <div><b><code>agentguard {name}</code></b><span>{body}</span></div>
    ))}
  </div>
  <p>Global flags: --store, --audit, --output, --secret-file. Use each command’s --help for arguments. The server is agentguard-server, not agentguard serve. Policy diff/version/blast-radius APIs live in the Rust library, not an agentguard policy command.</p>

  <h2>Framework compatibility</h2>
  <p>The Strands directory is a supported repository example using HTTP and a guard/intervention hook. The Rust example mounts build_router. Other frameworks can implement the same tool-boundary contract. There are no official LangChain, MCP, or Kubernetes adapters in these examples.</p>
  <p>Source references: <a href="https://github.com/sachncs/agent-guard/blob/master/typescript/agentguard/src/index.ts">TypeScript API</a>, <a href="https://github.com/sachncs/agent-guard/blob/master/crates/agentguard-cli/src/main.rs">CLI parser</a>, <a href="https://github.com/sachncs/agent-guard/blob/master/crates/agentguard-server/src/authzen.rs">HTTP request and response types</a>.</p>
</Docs>
